# guard/denylist.example - template for guard/denylist.local
#
# Copy this file to guard/denylist.local, then REPLACE the PLACEHOLDER lines in
# the "fill in" sections below with your own sensitive strings. denylist.local
# is gitignored on purpose: the whole point is that these strings never land in
# a committed file, and a committed denylist would defeat itself by naming them.
#
# THIS FILE SHIPS NO WORKING PATTERNS, so a verbatim copy does NOT pass the
# scan. Every non-comment line below is an ACTIVE PLACEHOLDER sentinel, and
# guard/scan.sh fails closed on any active PLACEHOLDER line. Structural markers
# (absolute home paths, note-vault paths, private-range and tailnet hosts,
# IBAN-shaped strings, and the like) are built into the scanner's unconditional
# PASS A, so you do NOT list them here. This file is only for the user-specific
# strings PASS A cannot guess: names, employer, clients, specific hostnames, and
# phone numbers.
#
# Two ways this stays fail-closed until you configure it: a raw copy still has
# active PLACEHOLDER sentinels (the scan FAILS on them), and deleting the
# sentinels without adding real patterns leaves zero active patterns (the scan
# FAILS on that too). Replace each PLACEHOLDER sentinel with your real patterns
# rather than merely deleting it.
#
# Format: one POSIX extended regular expression per line. Blank lines and lines
# starting with "#" are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive.
#
# Guard short names against false positives. BSD grep does not honor \b in an
# ERE, so wrap a short word like this instead:
#     (^|[^A-Za-z])NAME([^A-Za-z]|$)
# Escape dots in hostnames, or the dot matches any character:
#     internal-box\.example\.lan
# A bracketed first character (e.g. [U] instead of U) lets a pattern name a
# marker without this file literally containing that marker.
#
# guard/scan.sh FAILS the push if this list has zero active patterns or if any
# ACTIVE (non-comment) line still contains the token PLACEHOLDER, so REPLACE (do
# not merely delete) every PLACEHOLDER sentinel with your real patterns. The
# scanner ALSO catches the U+2014 em-dash directly, by its byte sequence, so no
# line here is needed for it (a literal em-dash could not be written into this
# file anyway).
#
# Run guard/scan.sh after editing. The pre-push hook runs it for you and refuses
# the push on any finding.

# --- FILL IN: family and personal names ---------------------------------------
# Every first name, surname, and nickname that appears in your notes: partner,
# children, and anyone whose name shows up in a memory filename. Replace the
# PLACEHOLDER line below with your patterns (one regex per line), then delete
# the PLACEHOLDER line. Example forms:
#   (^|[^A-Za-z])firstname([^A-Za-z]|$)
#   (^|[^A-Za-z])surname([^A-Za-z]|$)
PLACEHOLDER-REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FAMILY-AND-PERSONAL-NAMES

# --- FILL IN: employer and client names ---------------------------------------
# Current employer, previous employers still under NDA, and every client or
# prospect named in your working notes. Include common abbreviations and
# internal project codenames. Replace the PLACEHOLDER line below, then delete
# it:
#   (^|[^A-Za-z])your-employer([^A-Za-z]|$)
#   (^|[^A-Za-z])your-client([^A-Za-z]|$)
#   (^|[^A-Za-z])project-codename([^A-Za-z]|$)
PLACEHOLDER-REPLACE-WITH-EMPLOYER-AND-CLIENT-NAMES

# --- FILL IN: internal hostnames and networks ---------------------------------
# Machine names, VPN identifiers, and internal domains that identify one of your
# boxes. The generic tailnet and private-range forms are already covered by the
# scanner's PASS A; add your SPECIFIC ones here. Replace the PLACEHOLDER line
# below, then delete it:
#   your-laptop\.local
#   internal-box\.example\.lan
PLACEHOLDER-REPLACE-WITH-INTERNAL-HOSTNAMES-AND-NETWORKS

# --- FILL IN: phone numbers and account ids -----------------------------------
# Phone numbers in every format you write them (with and without country code,
# spaces, or dashes), plus chat ids, customer numbers, and membership numbers.
# Replace the PLACEHOLDER line below, then delete it:
#   \+?[0-9]{2}[ -]?[0-9]{3}[ -]?[0-9]{3}[ -]?[0-9]{3}
#   [0-9]{9,12}
PLACEHOLDER-REPLACE-WITH-PERSONAL-PHONE-AND-ACCOUNT-IDS
